      "summaries": {
        "en": "AI-Scientist-v2 is an open-source framework that automates scientific discovery by simulating how human researchers explore complex problems through systematic experimentation. Its core innovation is an agentic tree search algorithm where multiple AI agents collaboratively generate hypotheses, design experiments, and interpret results in branching decision trees. Researchers can use it to accelerate hypothesis testing in fields like materials science or drug discovery by configuring domain-specific knowledge bases and experimental constraints, enabling rapid exploration of solution spaces that would be impractical manually.",
        "zh": "AI-Scientist-v2是一个开源的科学发现自动化框架，它通过模拟人类研究者的系统性探索过程来解决复杂科学问题。该项目的核心技术是代理树搜索算法，多个AI代理在分支决策树中协作生成假设、设计实验并解释结果，这种架构模仿了科研团队的分工与迭代优化。用户可将其应用于材料科学或药物发现等领域，通过配置领域知识库和实验约束条件，快速探索传统方法难以覆盖的解决方案空间，为跨学科研究提供可扩展的自动化实验平台。",
        "es": "AI-Scientist-v2 is an open-source framework that automates scientific discovery by simulating how human researchers explore complex problems through systematic experimentation. Its core innovation is an agentic tree search algorithm where multiple AI agents collaboratively generate hypotheses, design experiments, and interpret results in branching decision trees. Researchers can use it to accelerate hypothesis testing in fields like materials science or drug discovery by configuring domain-specific knowledge bases and experimental constraints, enabling rapid exploration of solution spaces that would be impractical manually.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "AI-Scientist-v2 gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "AI-Scientist-v2 is an open-source framework that automates scientific discovery by simulating how human researchers explore complex problems through systematic experimentation. Its core innovation is an agentic tree search algorithm where multiple AI agents collaboratively generate hypotheses, design experiments, and interpret results in branching decision trees. Researchers can use it to accelerate hypothesis testing in fields like materials science or drug discovery by configuring domain-specific knowledge bases and experimental constraints, enabling rapid exploration of solution spaces that would be impractical manually.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/SakanaAI/AI-Scientist-v2 for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
